# A first `print` that calls a program function, at a stop in the entry's
# file, answers in under 250 ms on a program of 20,000 functions, as at a
# stop outside it (first_print_nonentry_under_250ms.case). The image is
# built where it is debugged, so its line table names the entry `./prog.jet`
# under the compilation directory `.`; the stop's source is still the
# snapshot's absolute prog.jet, so the session's held check of the
# package's cut gains f_1 (DebugCompile.jet jet_cli_debug_eval_held_append),
# or, while that check opens, the package's sources are compiled cut to the
# functions the expression reaches (jet_cli_debug_eval_sliced), not the
# program. Before, the two paths didn't
# match and the print opened the held check of the whole program: 1,846 ms
# (DebugLatency on the gate jet of p315).
# The print reads `total`, 0 at the stop, and calls f_1(x) = (x + 1) % 1000.
# gen/gen.jet writes prog.jet: run's first call, the stop, is line 100003.
fixture: SecondPrintAnswersUnder100ms.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run gen/gen.jet -- 20000
exit: 0
stdout: = ""
session debug line: jet debug prog.jet
env: PATH={work}/no-tools
send debug: "break prog.jet:100003"
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Breakpoint hit  prog.jet:100003  in run()" timeout 600s # the image builds and the program runs to the stop
send debug: "print f_1(total)"
recv debug line until ~ "f_1(total) = 1" within 250ms # the first print compiles only what it reaches
send debug: "c"
recv debug line until ~ "Program finished" timeout 600s # the evaluation left the program's run unchanged
close debug
exit: 0
